  "PlaceholderHidden": "hidden",
  "ProcessConfigFilterHover": "Data will be imported based on the values entered here. Regular expressions can be used.\nFor example, use\n\"\"   “abc” to search for items containing “abc” (partial match),\n   “^abc” to find items starting with “abc”,\n   “^abc$” for items matching “abc” (exact match),\n   “ab|c” to search for items containing either “ab” or “c” (OR condition), and\n   “^(?!test|abc).*” to find items starting something other than “test” or “abc”.\n(“^” indicates that the next character is at the beginning, “$” indicates that the preceding character is at the end, and “|” means OR.\nNote: The quotation marks are not needed when entering the values.)",
  "HoverConversationFormulaMsg": "Transformation rule used to define how judgment results are displayed.\nThis is used in graphs and other visualizations.\nWhen the data type is Judge, the formula (e.g., Pos=p0|p1, Neg=n1) is applied.\n\n- p0: Value of the positive case in the raw data (e.g., \"Pass\")\n- p1: Display value for the positive case (e.g., \"OK\")\n- n1: Display value for the negative case (e.g., \"NG\")\n\nValues that match p0 are transformed to p1;\nall other values are transformed to n1 for display.\nIf no positive case exists (e.g., defect history data), set p0 to Null.",
  "SelectJudgeDatatypeModalMsg": "Undefined judge value or more than three judge values found, automatic setting failed. Do you force it to be 'Judge'? (If so, please modify the conversion formula as appropriate)",
  "SelectJudgeDataTypeWarningFilterChangeModalMsg": "You will need to reset filter settings.",
